        "type": "text",
        "content": "You should remind clients to give prompt written notice of flood damage, even when they are unsure whether the loss is covered. The first notice should identify the loss location, contact details, flood depth, damage extent, coverage limits, lienholders, and any temporary address. They also must sign and submit a **proof of loss** with supporting documents within 60 days of loss, unless FEMA extends that deadline. If they seek Increased Cost of Compliance, they may need a separate proof of loss. ICC may apply when a community declares substantial damage and requires code compliance work."
      }
    ]
