        "content": "Proposals on **risk communication** would modernize maps, include future climate conditions, and require better flood-risk disclosures in residential transactions. They would also refine pricing by using replacement cost values and by separating coastal and inland flood classes. If adopted, these changes could help you explain risk more clearly to buyers, renters, and property owners."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "heading": "3.3.3 Resilience",
    "body_paragraphs": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The **resilience** proposals focus on long-term stability and loss reduction. They include a longer reauthorization period, a means-tested assistance program for qualifying households, revised treatment of excessive-loss properties, higher coverage limits, and a study of whether mandatory purchase rules are working. You can see how these ideas connect affordability with stronger mitigation and better targeting of assistance."
      }
