        "type": "text",
        "content": "With **comprehensive data**, regulators can better track availability, affordability, and market disruption. You should think of catastrophe modeling, geographic trend analysis, and multiyear data collection as tools for smarter decisions. Better data can help state insurance regulators set mitigation priorities, support funding requests, and understand how climate risks affect coverage options."
