        "content": "You should tell clients to give prompt written notice of flood damage, even when they are unsure the loss is covered. The first report should identify the property, contact information, location of loss, flood depth, damage areas, and any lienholder. They also must sign a **proof of loss**, or POL, within 60 days of the loss date unless FEMA grants more time."
      },
